# drivers/modem/conf: QMI, and the cellular modem.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver QMI
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.qmi.c
	help    QMI messages over the IPC router: how the Wi-Fi firmware's service and the modem's are spoken to

driver MODEM
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.mpss.c
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.cell.c
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.nas.c
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.ipa.c
	requires QMI UFS
	help    the modem (modem=1): started, its file systems served from the flash, the IPA's data path as en1,
	help    the SIM and the network registration. Research; needs fw-modem/ from the phone

driver SHANNON
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.shannon.c
	default n
	help    the Galaxy S9's own modem, the Shannon CP inside the Exynos 9810 (cp=N): 1 a look at its PMU words, its
	help    mailbox and the RADIO partition's table of contents; 2 its image copied from RADIO, read only and as it is,
	help    into the CP's memory at 0xF0000000 and checked by the secure world's own call; 3 the CP started, its boot
	help    loader's handshake, the ring table, PHONE_START; 4 the link, only with the phone's own NV data (cp_nv=1, a
	help    file the image's builder supplies; EFS is never read or written): "low power mode" asked first, the CP's
	help    messages logged, the software version asked; 5 with a ready SIM "normal" asked, the registration watched
	help    for two minutes, then low power again (written, not yet run: the test SIM read as locked). Its file
	help    requests are not answered. Only where the CP's memory is not XNU's (the ios-27 tree; not the 16.5 line's
	help    UEFI layout). Off unless asked
